<https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/latest-publications-and-news/#comparative-study-of-feature-selection-techniques-for-machine-learning-based> a schema:BlogPosting ;
    schema:abstract "Forecasting future solar power plant production is essential to continue the development of photovoltaic energy and increase its share in the energy mix for a more sustainable future. Accurate solar radiation forecasting greatly improves the balance maintenance between energy supply and demand and grid management performance. This study assesses the influence of input selection on short-term global horizontal irradiance (GHI) forecasting across two contrasting Algerian climates: arid Ghardaïa an",
        "Plusieurs techniques de sélection de variables comparées pour la prévision du rayonnement solaire par apprentissage automatique, dans les conditions climatiques algériennes." ;
    schema:author [ a schema:Person ;
            schema:name "Saïd Benkaciali" ],
        [ a schema:Person ;
            schema:name "Gilles Notton" ;
            schema:sameAs "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6267-9632" ],
        [ a schema:Person ;
            schema:name "Saïd Benkaciali" ],
        [ a schema:Person ;
            schema:name "Gilles Notton" ;
            schema:sameAs "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6267-9632" ],
        <https://person.cyrilvoyant.com/#cyril-voyant> ;
    schema:datePublished "2025-07-12" ;
    schema:headline "Comparative Study of Feature Selection Techniques for Machine Learning-Based Solar Irradiation Forecasting to Facilitate the Sustainable Development of Photovoltaics: Application to Algerian Climatic Conditions",
        "Sélection des variables d'entrée pour prévoir le rayonnement solaire par apprentissage automatique : cas de l'Algérie" ;
    schema:image "https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/assets/img/98c7979fb52e.png" ;
    schema:inLanguage "en" ;
    schema:url "https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/latest-publications-and-news/#comparative-study-of-feature-selection-techniques-for-machine-learning-based" .

<https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/latest-publications-and-news/#electre-carnot-mines-electrification> a schema:BlogPosting ;
    schema:abstract "ELECTRE brings together about fifteen laboratories, centres and institutes of the Carnot M.I.N.E.S institute around 13 research projects (2023–2026) on the electrification of uses, from materials to storage, industrial processes and the limits of electrification. Its closing workshop is on 18 November 2026, Mines Paris – PSL, Sophia Antipolis.",
        "ELECTRE fédère une quinzaine de laboratoires, centres et instituts de l'institut Carnot M.I.N.E.S autour de 13 projets de recherche (2023-2026) sur l'électrification des usages, des matériaux au stockage, aux procédés industriels et aux limites de l'électrification. Sa journée de clôture a lieu le 18 novembre 2026 à Mines Paris – PSL, Sophia Antipolis." ;
    schema:author [ a schema:Person ;
            schema:name "Delphine Gilges-Crampont" ],
        [ a schema:Person ;
