<https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/latest-publications-and-news/#from-pixels-to-tolerances-rethinking-forecast-validation-with-the-index> a schema:BlogPosting ;
    schema:abstract "Classical metrics like RMSE evaluate forecasts as if every pixel must match perfectly in space and time. Machines optimize for that. Humans do not think that way.",
        "Les métriques classiques comme le RMSE jugent une prévision comme si chaque pixel devait coïncider parfaitement dans l'espace et le temps. L'indice γ accepte un décalage toléré, comme le fait un expert." ;
    schema:author <https://person.cyrilvoyant.com/#cyril-voyant> ;
    schema:datePublished "2026-03-28" ;
    schema:headline "Des pixels aux tolérances : valider les prévisions avec l'indice γ",
        "From Pixels to Tolerances: Rethinking Forecast Validation with the γ-Index" ;
    schema:image "https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/assets/img/7f20ac04a02f.png" ;
    schema:inLanguage "en" ;
    schema:url "https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/latest-publications-and-news/#from-pixels-to-tolerances-rethinking-forecast-validation-with-the-index" .

<https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/latest-publications-and-news/#from-trends-to-insights-a-text-mining-analysis-of-solar-energy-forecasting-2017> a schema:BlogPosting ;
    schema:abstract "La fouille de textes de 500 articles cartographie la recherche mondiale en prévision solaire : forte montée de l'IA et de l'apprentissage profond, portée par la Chine, les États-Unis et l'Inde, et métriques déterministes encore dominantes.",
        "The study applies text mining to 500 papers (2017–2023) to map global trends in solar energy forecasting. It reveals a strong rise of AI and deep learning, led by China, the USA, and India, and shows that deterministic metrics still dominate probabilistic ones. The work delivers a reproducible overview and standardized terminology, advancing transparency and collaboration in solar forecasting research ." ;
    schema:author [ a schema:Person ;
            schema:name "Mohammed Asloune" ;
            schema:sameAs "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-0183-2156" ],
