<https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/latest-publications-and-news/#on-the-importance-of-clearsky-model-in-short-term-solar-radiation-forecasting> a schema:BlogPosting ;
    schema:abstract "Clearsky models are widely used in solar energy for many applications such as quality control, resource assessment, satellite-base irradiance estimation and forecasting. However, their use in forecasting and nowcasting is associated with a number of challenges. Synchronization errors, reliance on the Clearsky index (ratio of the global horizontal irradiance to its cloud-free counterpart) and high sensitivity of the clearsky model to errors in aerosol optical depth at low solar elevation limit th",
        "Les modèles de ciel clair servent partout en énergie solaire, mais leur usage en prévision pose des difficultés : erreurs de synchronisation, choix de l'indice de ciel clair, effets sur les scores." ;
    schema:author [ a schema:Person ;
            schema:name "Gilles Notton" ;
            schema:sameAs "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6267-9632" ],
