<https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/latest-publications-and-news/#transfer-learning-for-wind-speed-forecasting-a-scalable-approach-for-data> a schema:BlogPosting ;
    schema:abstract "Réutiliser des modèles entraînés sur des sites riches en données permet de prévoir la vitesse du vent sur des sites qui en ont peu : sur 4 830 expériences, une précision comparable à l'apprentissage direct (écart de nRMSE inférieur à 0,01).",
        "This paper demonstrates that transfer learning can accurately forecast wind speed in data-scarce regions by reusing models trained on data-rich sites. Across 4,830 experiments, TL achieved accuracy comparable to direct learning (ΔnRMSE < 0.01). The approach offers a scalable, low-data solution for expanding wind forecasting to under-instrumented areas." ;
    schema:author [ a schema:Person ;
            schema:name "Gilles Notton" ;
            schema:sameAs "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6267-9632" ],
        [ a schema:Person ;
            schema:name "Milan Despotović" ;
            schema:sameAs "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3144-5945" ],
        [ a schema:Person ;
            schema:name "Gilles Notton" ;
            schema:sameAs "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6267-9632" ],
        [ a schema:Person ;
            schema:name "Milan Despotović" ;
            schema:sameAs "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3144-5945" ],
        <https://person.cyrilvoyant.com/#cyril-voyant> ;
    schema:datePublished "2025-10-13" ;
    schema:headline "Apprentissage par transfert pour prévoir le vent là où les données manquent",
        "Transfer Learning for Wind Speed Forecasting: A Scalable Approach for Data-Scarce Environments" ;
    schema:image "https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/assets/img/435a8e9d3433.png" ;
    schema:inLanguage "en" ;
    schema:url "https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/latest-publications-and-news/#transfer-learning-for-wind-speed-forecasting-a-scalable-approach-for-data" .

<https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/latest-publications-and-news/#tunnel-load-simulator-an-open-source-generator-for-synthetic-road-tunnel> a schema:BlogPosting ;
    schema:abstract "Application libre (Streamlit), développée dans le projet SmartTunnel, qui produit des profils de charge électrique synthétiques pour les tunnels routiers : éclairage, ventilation, auxiliaires, trafic, saisons et événements aléatoires.",
        "The Tunnel Load Simulator is an open-source Streamlit application developed within the SmartTunnel project to generate synthetic electrical load profiles for road tunnels. It combines simplified representations of lighting, ventilation, auxiliary loads, traffic patterns, seasonal effects and stochastic events such as pollution episodes or accidents." ;
    schema:author <https://person.cyrilvoyant.com/#cyril-voyant> ;
    schema:datePublished "2026-05-08" ;
    schema:headline "Tunnel Load Simulator : générer la consommation électrique des tunnels routiers",
        "Tunnel Load Simulator: an open-source generator for synthetic road-tunnel electricity demand" ;
    schema:image "https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/assets/img/e326492cab74.jpg" ;
    schema:inLanguage "en" ;
    schema:url "https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/latest-publications-and-news/#tunnel-load-simulator-an-open-source-generator-for-synthetic-road-tunnel" .

